{
  "pack_id": "flask-sqlite3",
  "schema_version": 2,
  "authored_from": "framework_docs",
  "extends": "_base",
  "description": "The hand-written reference pack: Flask + Flask-Login + Flask-SQLAlchemy + WTForms + sqlite3 vocabulary, from their documentation. Adds to _base; never removes. Selected automatically when the target imports flask or lists it in requirements.txt. 2026-09-15: scoped-query tokens added after the O3 rehearsal (the LLM's canonical Flask fix binds g.user.id into the WHERE clause).",
  "sources": ["https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/api/  (request.args / values / get_json / form.to_dict, abort)", "https://flask-login.readthedocs.io/en/latest/  (current_user, login_required, fresh_login_required, get_id)", "https://flask-sqlalchemy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/queries/  (get_or_404, first_or_404, one_or_none, session.commit/flush, query.update)", "https://wtforms.readthedocs.io/en/stable/  (populate_obj, validate_on_submit, NumberRange)", "https://docs.python.org/3/library/sqlite3.html  (executemany, executescript, isolation_level, BEGIN IMMEDIATE/EXCLUSIVE, REPLACE)", "https://flask-principal.readthedocs.io/  (permission.require, permission.can)", "https://flask-security-too.readthedocs.io/  (roles_required, roles_accepted)"],
  "slots": {
    "authz_guard": {
      "sink": "guard_text",
      "values": ["current_user.id ==", "== current_user.id", "current_user.id !=", "!= current_user.id", "current_user.get_id() ==", "== current_user.get_id()", "roles_required", "roles_accepted", "permission.require", "permission.can", "current_user.is_admin", "current_user.has_role", ", g.user.id)", ", g.user.id,", "(g.user.id,", ", current_user.id)", ", current_user.id,", "(current_user.id,", ", g.user[\"id\"])", ", session[\"user_id\"])"],
      "note": "The Flask-Login ownership idiom is `if order.user_id != current_user.id: abort(403)`. The comparison operands are what proves the check exists; `current_user` alone proves only login and stays in authn_only. Operands are matched in both orders. Scoped raw SQL: the current user's id passed INTO the query's parameter tuple (`(order_id, g.user.id)`, `(order_id, current_user.id)`) is the sqlite3 form of `owner=request.user`; the tokens require the comma/paren context so a bare g.user (authn) never matches."
    },
    "authn_only": {
      "sink": "guard_text",
      "values": ["fresh_login_required", "flask_login", "login_manager", "verify_password", "auth.login_required", "session.pop(", "current_user.is_authenticated"]
    },
    "lock_guard": {
      "sink": "guard_text",
      "values": ["begin immediate", "begin exclusive", "isolation_level", "session.begin_nested", "with_for_update("]
    },
    "allowlist_guard": {
      "sink": "guard_text",
      "values": ["validate_on_submit", "form.validate", "schema.load(", "only=(", "only=[", "fields=(", "fields=[", "load_only", "exclude=("],
      "note": "A WTForm or a marshmallow schema declares its fields, so writing through one is an allow-list by construction."
    },
    "positive_guard": {
      "sink": "guard_text",
      "values": ["numberrange(", "min=1", "min=0", "> 0.0", ">= 1"]
    },
    "mass_assign_signal": {
      "sink": "signal_text",
      "values": ["request.args", "request.values", "request.get_json", "form.to_dict", "request.data", "**form"]
    },
    "qty_terms": {
      "sink": "token",
      "values": ["units", "num_items"]
    },
    "price_terms": {
      "sink": "token",
      "values": ["cost", "credit", "discount", "refund"]
    },
    "orm_read_calls": {
      "sink": "call_name",
      "values": ["get_or_404", "first_or_404", "one_or_none", "scalar_one", "scalar_one_or_none"],
      "note": "Not `get`: dict.get / request.args.get would make every method with an id parameter a candidate."
    },
    "dyn_write_calls": {
      "sink": "call_name",
      "values": ["update", "populate_obj"]
    },
    "commit_calls": {
      "sink": "call_name",
      "values": ["flush"]
    },
    "exec_calls": {
      "sink": "call_name",
      "values": ["executemany", "executescript"]
    },
    "sql_write_kw": {
      "sink": "exec_sql_kw",
      "values": ["REPLACE"]
    },
    "id_param_exact": {
      "sink": "param_exact",
      "values": ["pk", "uid", "slug", "uuid"]
    },
    "id_param_suffix": {
      "sink": "param_suffix",
      "values": ["_pk", "_uuid", "_slug", "_no", "_num"]
    },
    "route_markers": {
      "sink": "signal_text",
      "values": [".get(\"", ".post(\"", ".put(\"", ".patch(\"", ".delete(\"", "add_url_rule(", ".route("],
      "note": "P7. Flask 2+ method shortcuts (@app.get(\"/x\")) and add_url_rule; the quote keeps dict.get( out."
    }
  }
}
